00029:   "immutable_policy": "Original 43761B/810de fact container and all original manifest files remain unchanged; use complete corrected object as mandatory companion to original full fact, preserving old text and counterreading trail. No silent original rewrite.",
00030:   "erroneous_field": "/facts/7/meaning/4",
00031:   "old_exact_field": "HalfHP EmergencyExit/WimpOut: wild branch requires actual escape permission (and opposing wild has no multiple living same-side restriction); writes decision3 after reached audio/message. Trainer branch checks foes/switch/nonactive then EOR recalls/leaves with no immediate replacement. Remaining full escape policy and existing C0122 faint/presentation closures stay with root actual readers.",
00032:   "old_full_fact": "old-fact.complete.json",
00033:   "corrected_full_fact": "corrected-fact.complete.json",
00034:   "only_fact_change": "meaning[4] only; all other original ERT-ITEM-PIPE object fields retained byte-equivalent as parsed JSON values.",
00035:   "why_wrong": "The words has no multiple living same-side restriction deny a guard that source explicitly imposes on an opposing bearer: current live same-side count>1 returnsfalse. The helper counts living nonnil same-side objects, not total seats or party reserves.",
00036:   "strongest_alternative_interpretations": [
00037:     {
00038:       "interpretation": "No multiple living could have been intended to mean that opposing wild must be alone.",
00039:       "disposition": "Rejected as defense of the actual old wording: has no ... restriction explicitly describes absence of restriction, and no single-living precondition is stated. Corrected object states the actual rejection gate."
00040:     },
00041:     {
00042:       "interpretation": "The rule might concern player-side EmergencyExit in a wild battle.",
00043:       "disposition": "That player-side contrast is source-supported for this population guard only, but does not rescue the old sentence explicitly saying opposing wild. Shared escape permission still applies."
00044:     },
00045:     {
00046:       "interpretation": "Two occupied wild slots imply count2 even if one has fainted.",
00047:       "disposition": "Rejected: allSameSideBattlers filters fainted/nil, so one live plus one fainted gives1 and passes this gate."
00048:     }
00049:   ],
